Zero the copies a secret pipeline write leaves behind

Pipeline::write_secret queues the same Twrite frame as write, then
zeroes the request body once it is queued and the output buffer's spare
capacity after each send until the buffer has emptied; dropping the
pipeline first zeroes the whole buffer. Draining sent bytes moves the
unsent tail forward, so the vacated bytes would otherwise stay in the
allocation for the life of the connection.

Sophia's session lock sends the unlock password to its authentication
agent through this pipeline (t034 security review, finding 3).
